{# Engagement block — explains the 3-rung ladder (Read / Contribute / Propose).
   v1 routes Contribute and Propose through GitHub PRs. React (upvote/bookmark/flag)
   is deferred to v2 when there's a database backend.

   Usage: {% include "partials/engagement-block.njk" %}
   Optional: set `engagementContext` in frontmatter to a short string
   (e.g., "for this domain") to localize the block.
#}

<aside class="engagement-block" aria-label="How to engage">
  <h2 class="engagement-block__heading">Verify &amp; contribute{% if engagementContext %} <span class="engagement-block__context">{{ engagementContext }}</span>{% endif %}</h2>
  <p class="engagement-block__lead">
    This project gets better when readers push back on it. Every page is editable, every change is tracked, every contributor is credited at whatever level of identity they choose.
  </p>

  <ol class="engagement-block__ladder">
    <li class="rung rung--read">
      <h3>Read</h3>
      <p>No account needed. Read anything on the site, follow citations, decide for yourself whether the analysis holds.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="rung rung--contribute">
      <h3>Contribute</h3>
      <p>Spot a factual error, missing source, or framing problem? Open a pull request on GitHub. Quick fixes, source additions, narrative edits — all welcome.</p>
      <p class="rung__action">
        <a href="/paul/campaign/empower/contribute/">How to contribute →</a>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="rung rung--propose">
      <h3>Propose</h3>
      <p>Bigger ideas — a new sub-domain analysis, a constituent profile, a policy proposal — go through a longer review. Same PR mechanism, more conversation around it.</p>
      <p class="rung__action">
        <a href="/paul/campaign/empower/contribute/#propose">How to propose →</a>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="engagement-block__privacy">
    Privacy: every contribution is attributed at the level you pick — anonymous, first name + neighborhood, full name + neighborhood, or full name with link. <a href="/paul/campaign/empower/contribute/#privacy">Privacy options →</a>
  </p>
</aside>
